SpiderMonkey on 64-bit SPARC illumos: run in a 32-bit address space.

JS::Value (NaN boxing, JSVAL_TAG_SHIFT 47) needs every pointer it holds to
have the top 16 bits clear (Value.h IsValidUserModePointer); that covers
private pointers too, not only the GC heap. 64-bit illumos/Solaris on SPARC
puts the stack, shared libraries and mmap() memory just below
0xFFFFFFFF80000000, so such pointers break the boxing at run time.

Mozilla bug 577056 ("Memory layout for 64-bit Solaris is different than
other 64-bit systems"): https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=577056
Oracle Solaris reserves the upper address range with a RESERVE_SEGMENT
mapfile in each program (oracle/solaris-userland gjs and gnome-shell); the
illumos link-editor has no RESERVE_SEGMENT. It has the SF1_SUNW_ADDR32
software capability: an executable tagged ADDR32 runs with USERLIMIT32,
its stack below 4 GB, and the runtime linker refuses a shared object
tagged ADDR32 in any process that is not.

Tag libmozjs and the js shell. Programs linking libmozjs (gjs-console,
gnome-shell) must be tagged ADDR32 as well; ld warns when they are not.
Only for TARGET_CPU sparc64, so other platforms are unchanged.

Upstream status: to be reported to Mozilla (bugzilla.mozilla.org).

--- a/js/src/build/moz.build
+++ b/js/src/build/moz.build
@@ -82,6 +82,9 @@
         "nsl",
         "socket",
     ]
+    # Values need 47-bit pointers: keep sparc64 processes below 4 GB (bug 577056)
+    if CONFIG["TARGET_CPU"] == "sparc64" and CONFIG["JS_SHARED_LIBRARY"]:
+        LDFLAGS += ["-Wl,-M,%s/sparc-addr32.mapfile" % SRCDIR]
 
 if CONFIG["OS_ARCH"] == "WINNT":
     OS_LIBS += [
--- /dev/null
+++ b/js/src/build/sparc-addr32.mapfile
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+#
+# This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
+# License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
+# file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
+#
+# illumos/Solaris sparc64: run in a 32-bit address space (ADDR32)
+#
+$mapfile_version 2
+CAPABILITY {
+	SF += ADDR32;
+};
--- a/js/src/shell/moz.build
+++ b/js/src/shell/moz.build
@@ -59,6 +59,10 @@
     LDFLAGS += ["-Wl,-z,stack-size=1048576", "-Wl,--stack-first"]
     OS_LIBS += ["wasi-emulated-process-clocks", "wasi-emulated-getpid"]
 
+# sparc64: 32-bit address space, see js/src/build/moz.build
+if CONFIG["OS_ARCH"] == "SunOS" and CONFIG["TARGET_CPU"] == "sparc64":
+    LDFLAGS += ["-Wl,-M,%s/js/src/build/sparc-addr32.mapfile" % TOPSRCDIR]
+
 # Make JS Shell builds run without LD_LIBRARY_PATH
 if CONFIG["OS_TARGET"] == "Android":
     LDFLAGS += [
